course: dictionary
lesson: 8752
title: One word, many meanings: setting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Setting» is one of them. When you meet it, read the words around it to find which meaning fits. Ask yourself: what is this word doing in this sentence?
explain: «Every story has characters (who), a setting (where and when) and a plot (what happens).» Here the clues are story, where and when. So setting means the place and time where the story happens.
explain: «Safe search is a setting that filters out adult results when you search.» The clues are device, filters and search. So here a setting is a control you can change, like a switch on a phone or tablet.
explain: «The sun is setting over the hills.» The word sun and the time of day are your clues. Setting here is the -ing form of set, so it means going down. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Setting can mean the place and time where a story happens.
fact: Setting can mean a control on a machine, such as the heat on an oven or the volume on a phone.
fact: A place setting is the knife, fork, plate and glass for one person at a table.
fact: «A lovely setting by the lake» means the surroundings of something.
fact: «The sun is setting» uses the -ing form of set, which means going down.
exercise: «Every story has characters, a setting and a plot.» In this sentence, what does setting mean? | *The place and time where the story happens | The knife and fork for one person | The sun going down | The brightness on a phone
exercise: «Safe search is a setting that filters out adult results.» Here a setting is | *A control you can change, like a switch | A place where a story happens | A plate and glass at the table | The sun going down
exercise: «The sun is setting over the hills.» What does setting mean here? | A place and time for a story | The plate and glass for one person | A volume control | *Going down, towards the horizon
test: «Set the table with a place setting for each person.» What is a place setting? | The -ing form of sun | The beautiful surroundings of a lake | *The knife, fork, plate and glass for one person | The heat on the oven
test: «The story's setting is a castle long ago.» What does setting mean? | *Where and when the story happens | The plate and glass for one person | The surroundings of the castle | A control on a machine
exam: «The oven was on a low setting, so the cake baked slowly.» What does setting mean? | *A position of a control on a machine | The plate and glass for one person | The -ing form of set | The place and time where a story happens
